{"id":27901,"slug":"anatomy-of-a-murder","title":"Anatomy of a Murder","year":1959,"country":"United States","duration":161,"spine":600,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27901-anatomy-of-a-murder","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/303871dba84408054692162d362e800f/DZ4pikcV8PR878mzRBY3nRygvVnyXH_large.jpg","description":"A virtuoso James Stewart plays a small-town Michigan lawyer who takes on a difficult case: the defense of a young army lieutenant (Ben Gazzara) accused of murdering a local tavern owner who he believes raped his wife (Lee Remick). This gripping envelope-pusher, the most popular film by Hollywood provocateur Otto Preminger, was groundbreaking for the frankness of its discussion of sex—but more than anything else, it is a striking depiction of the power of words. Featuring an outstanding supporting cast—with a young George C. Scott as a fiery prosecutor and the legendary attorney Joseph N. Welch as the judge—and an influential score by Duke Ellington, Anatomy of a Murder is an American movie landmark, nominated for seven Oscars, including best picture.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Otto Preminger","slug":"otto-preminger"}],"cast":[{"actor":"James Stewart","role":"Paul Biegler","slug":"james-stewart"},{"actor":"Lee Remick","role":"Laura Manion","slug":"lee-remick"},{"actor":"Ben Gazzara","role":"Lieutenant Frederick Manion","slug":"ben-gazzara"},{"actor":"Arthur O'Connell","role":"Parnell McCarthy","slug":"arthur-o-connell"},{"actor":"Eve Arden","role":"Maida Rutledge","slug":"eve-arden"},{"actor":"Kathryn Grant","role":"Mary Pilant","slug":"kathryn-grant"},{"actor":"George C. Scott","role":"Claude Dancer","slug":"george-c-scott"},{"actor":"Orson Bean","role":"Dr. Matthew Smith","slug":"orson-bean"},{"actor":"Russ Brown","role":"George Lemon","slug":"russ-brown"},{"actor":"Murray Hamilton","role":"Alphonse Paquette","slug":"murray-hamilton"},{"actor":"Brooks West","role":"Mitch Lodwick","slug":"brooks-west"